(762122, 81132, 11078, '<td valign="top">Wow what a beautiful image You really deserve the blue ribbon Well taken and such a lovely place Congratulations Jodie I also think your profile shot is lovely</td>', 'Wow what a beautiful image You really deserve the blue ribbon Well taken and such a lovely place Congratulations Jodie I also think your profile shot is lovely', '2004-06-14 01:36:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(762131, 81132, 17148, '<td valign="top">I called it, I knew this would win, now I don''t have to cry...by the way your "Loud!" photo was my first favorite added on this site, and this is my 47th. Great work!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-14 00:41:49.</i></td>', 'I called it, I knew this would win, now I don''t have to cry...by the way your "Loud!" photo was my first favorite added on this site, and this is my 47th. Great work!!', '2004-06-14 01:40:12.000000', '2004-06-14 01:41:49.000000', 0),
(762132, 81132, 8054, '<td valign="top">This was my 1st place choice although it was very tough work voting. Congratulations on your first place ribbon!</td>', 'This was my 1st place choice although it was very tough work voting. Congratulations on your first place ribbon!', '2004-06-14 01:41:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(762135, 81312, 5112, '<td valign="top">David,<br/> <br/>I was wondering whose picture this was.  I thought Colorado (I guess the title threw me for a loop).  It''s beautiful.<br/> <br/>I''ve been trying to PM a thank you note to you, but there seems to be something funny going on with PMs.  So ... thank you so much for the write up earlier today.  It was such a beautiful surprise.  It means A LOT to me.  Thanks!<br/> <br/>Ursula</td>', 'David, I was wondering whose picture this was.  I thought Colorado (I guess the title threw me for a loop).  It''s beautiful. I''ve been trying to PM a thank you note to you, but there seems to be something funny going on with PMs.  So ... thank you so much for the write up earlier today.  It was such a beautiful surprise.  It means A LOT to me.  Thanks! Ursula', '2004-06-14 01:42:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(762142, 81902, 5112, '<td valign="top">I just knew this was Iceland!  What a beautiful photo.  The clouds kind of follow the shape of the horses.  I love it!</td>', 'I just knew this was Iceland!  What a beautiful photo.  The clouds kind of follow the shape of the horses.  I love it!', '2004-06-14 01:45:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(762156, 80655, 5112, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!  Great example of deep DOF, and a beautiful guitar.  <br/> <br/></td>', 'Congratulations!  Great example of deep DOF, and a beautiful guitar.   ', '2004-06-14 01:51:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(762161, 81132, 10055, '<td valign="top">Congrats!!! I had a feelling that this shot would be in the top 5, hey it''s the Blue, cool!</td>', 'Congrats!!! I had a feelling that this shot would be in the top 5, hey it''s the Blue, cool!', '2004-06-14 01:53:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(762164, 80655, 10055, '<td valign="top">Congrats</td>', 'Congrats', '2004-06-14 01:54:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(762167, 81493, 7322, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 7. It should have done much better,certainly better than my own (which I thought should have done better than it did...:-D). It was one of my top picks.</td>', 'I gave this a 7. It should have done much better,certainly better than my own (which I thought should have done better than it did...:-D). It was one of my top picks.', '2004-06-14 01:56:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(762175, 81372, 7322, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6. It should have done much better than this. The placement of the girl in the center was well-considered and works wonderfully to draw your eye into the scene she is viewing. The motion blur of the skaters adds excitement and the skaters in the distance and the folks waiting on the benches add to the depth of the scene. I think the reason I didn''t score it higher was I thought there was a bit too much blurring of the wall in the foreground. If you cropped some of that (just a tiny bit) the girl would be dead center and the shot would really be fantastic, IMO. As i is it''s a really cool and interesting shot. You should be proud of this one.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-14 01:05:59.</i></td>', 'I gave this a 6. It should have done much better than this. The placement of the girl in the center was well-considered and works wonderfully to draw your eye into the scene she is viewing. The motion blur of the skaters adds excitement and the skaters in the distance and the folks waiting on the benches add to the depth of the scene. I think the reason I didn''t score it higher was I thought there was a bit too much blurring of the wall in the foreground. If you cropped some of that (just a tiny bit) the girl would be dead center and the shot would really be fantastic, IMO. As i is it''s a really cool and interesting shot. You should be proud of this one.', '2004-06-14 02:03:58.000000', '2004-06-14 02:05:59.000000', 0),
(762176, 81132, 70, '<td valign="top">This is amazing! What a great sense of wide open space it gives in such a relatively small picture. Beautiful.</td>', 'This is amazing! What a great sense of wide open space it gives in such a relatively small picture. Beautiful.', '2004-06-14 02:05:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(762184, 81069, 13336, '<td valign="top">this image is absolutely stunning.<br/> <br/>i''m assuming you used some kind of flash to expose the first tree while setting the camera to expose for the sky...?</td>', 'this image is absolutely stunning. i''m assuming you used some kind of flash to expose the first tree while setting the camera to expose for the sky...?', '2004-06-14 02:09:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(762192, 81069, 714, '<td valign="top">Wow, Spaz!  Awesome shot here!  Congrats!</td>', 'Wow, Spaz!  Awesome shot here!  Congrats!', '2004-06-14 02:13:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(762200, 80655, 6073, '<td valign="top">How this is 2nd???? I dunno</td>', 'How this is 2nd???? I dunno', '2004-06-14 02:18:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(762211, 81069, 10686, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by darcy:</b></div><hr/><i> this image is absolutely stunning.<br/> <br/>i''m assuming you used some kind of flash to expose the first tree while setting the camera to expose for the sky...? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you. <br/> <br/>No flash, just a bit of dodging on the tree and a bit of burning on the sky.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-14 01:25:03.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by darcy: this image is absolutely stunning. i''m assuming you used some kind of flash to expose the first tree while setting the camera to expose for the sky...?   Thank you.  No flash, just a bit of dodging on the tree and a bit of burning on the sky.', '2004-06-14 02:23:32.000000', '2004-06-14 02:25:03.000000', 0),
