(762473, 81069, 16148, '<td valign="top">Great shot!  I didn''t have a chance to go through all the pictures during voting and missed yours.  Very interesting perspective and nice use of deep depth of field.  Congradulations on your ribbon.</td>', 'Great shot!  I didn''t have a chance to go through all the pictures during voting and missed yours.  Very interesting perspective and nice use of deep depth of field.  Congradulations on your ribbon.', '2004-06-14 08:35:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(762490, 81557, 14614, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the *very* helpful comments.  I didn''t take the time to neatimage the sky (I thought it would fuzz up the building and lose some dof) but clearly I should have!</td>', 'Thanks for all the *very* helpful comments.  I didn''t take the time to neatimage the sky (I thought it would fuzz up the building and lose some dof) but clearly I should have!', '2004-06-14 08:52:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(762496, 81507, 22083, '<td valign="top">What can I say I really brain farted on this one. When I saw DEEP I was think just the opposite.  As most of you noted in your comments.</td>', 'What can I say I really brain farted on this one. When I saw DEEP I was think just the opposite.  As most of you noted in your comments.', '2004-06-14 09:02:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(762497, 81528, 6999, '<td valign="top">I was almost convinced this was a jjbeguin shot - to the extent of being surprised it isn''t. It has his trick with colours, and the shaping and shading of those foreground leaves. Also this composition is very typical of some of his work from a little while ago. Interesting stuff Dan; and it remains (as my previous comment meant to emphasise more) an abject lesson in how only a very small thing can have a disproportionate effect on an image - that tree can take up no more than about 3% of this image.</td>', 'I was almost convinced this was a jjbeguin shot - to the extent of being surprised it isn''t. It has his trick with colours, and the shaping and shading of those foreground leaves. Also this composition is very typical of some of his work from a little while ago. Interesting stuff Dan; and it remains (as my previous comment meant to emphasise more) an abject lesson in how only a very small thing can have a disproportionate effect on an image - that tree can take up no more than about 3% of this image.', '2004-06-14 09:03:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(762502, 81186, 22239, '<td valign="top">I have another version of this that''s much cleaner... I never seem to have enough time to work with these things in post. :D<br/> <br/>/Andrew<br/></td>', 'I have another version of this that''s much cleaner... I never seem to have enough time to work with these things in post. :D /Andrew', '2004-06-14 09:10:36.000000', NULL, 0),
