(764051, 81181, 22734, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :) <br/>  First: Congratulations on your good image. The composition and technical aspect are almost beyond question. When I first looked at your study, it gave me the subtle feeling that the sky was pressing down on the strip of land and cityscape. Upon closer examination I would have chosen to correct the horizon. This would also place the pole parallel to the right side of the picture. In pictures like this, the horizon is critical. By making it straight it gives the base the stability it needs to offset the overwhelming sky. With so much sky. you do not want anybody to question the line of division betweem sky and land.<br/> Of course, the sky is beautiful and I can tell by your shooting angle that this was the effect you sought. Keep up the good work.  dan<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :)   First: Congratulations on your good image. The composition and technical aspect are almost beyond question. When I first looked at your study, it gave me the subtle feeling that the sky was pressing down on the strip of land and cityscape. Upon closer examination I would have chosen to correct the horizon. This would also place the pole parallel to the right side of the picture. In pictures like this, the horizon is critical. By making it straight it gives the base the stability it needs to offset the overwhelming sky. With so much sky. you do not want anybody to question the line of division betweem sky and land. Of course, the sky is beautiful and I can tell by your shooting angle that this was the effect you sought. Keep up the good work.  dan', '2004-06-15 14:57:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(764064, 81132, 22970, '<td valign="top">Hi everyone! This is my first post on DPChallenge and what a wonderful picture to post too. Please forgive me if I over speak but I think this is a wonderful picture. I hope to have the nerve to get involved in a challenge in the near future. I am taking time to read the rules, back to the picture at hand. I love the depth of field form the stones in the lake below the water to the mountaintops as far as the eye can see. It is truly a picture of tranquility. I love the way the dock tilts towards the right as if its following the lakes curve. Great Photo.</td>', 'Hi everyone! This is my first post on DPChallenge and what a wonderful picture to post too. Please forgive me if I over speak but I think this is a wonderful picture. I hope to have the nerve to get involved in a challenge in the near future. I am taking time to read the rules, back to the picture at hand. I love the depth of field form the stones in the lake below the water to the mountaintops as far as the eye can see. It is truly a picture of tranquility. I love the way the dock tilts towards the right as if its following the lakes curve. Great Photo.', '2004-06-15 15:23:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(764161, 81132, 10444, '<td valign="top">jodie!! your picture is so fabulous, and brings back many happy memories of glacier for me. i lived &amp; worked in the park in 1195 &amp; 1996. i love the northfork area, where kintla is...polebridge has a special place in my heart, too. thanks again for this...and congratulations!!!!!!!<br/>melanie<br/>melanie@dreambigarts.com</td>', 'jodie!! your picture is so fabulous, and brings back many happy memories of glacier for me. i lived & worked in the park in 1195 & 1996. i love the northfork area, where kintla is...polebridge has a special place in my heart, too. thanks again for this...and congratulations!!!!!!!melaniemelanie@dreambigarts.com', '2004-06-15 16:41:57.000000', NULL, 0),
