(764653, 81132, 9534, '<td valign="top">Unbelievable! This is a stunning composition, AWESOME depth of field.<br/>Next time (and try with this file if you still have the native file) use "High Pass" for sharpening. I can''t imagine this being any better than it is right now, but if anything could do it, that would.<br/> <br/>Congratulations and BRAVO!!!!!<br/> <br/>Peggy Bjarno</td>', 'Unbelievable! This is a stunning composition, AWESOME depth of field.Next time (and try with this file if you still have the native file) use "High Pass" for sharpening. I can''t imagine this being any better than it is right now, but if anything could do it, that would. Congratulations and BRAVO!!!!! Peggy Bjarno', '2004-06-15 23:18:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(764658, 80655, 9534, '<td valign="top">HOW?????? I cannot imagine . . . it''s one thing to get it all in focus in a landscape, but in a STILL LIFE like this???? NO . . . how . . . .?<br/> <br/>Genius! <br/> <br/>Great job, and congratulations,<br/>Peggy</td>', 'HOW?????? I cannot imagine . . . it''s one thing to get it all in focus in a landscape, but in a STILL LIFE like this???? NO . . . how . . . .? Genius!  Great job, and congratulations,Peggy', '2004-06-15 23:20:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(764665, 81069, 9534, '<td valign="top">Did you use a flash? Did you layer it? This is so incredible I cannot imagine . . . <br/> <br/>GREAT job! Good eye, good editing, and congratulations!<br/> <br/>Peggy</td>', 'Did you use a flash? Did you layer it? This is so incredible I cannot imagine . . .  GREAT job! Good eye, good editing, and congratulations! Peggy', '2004-06-15 23:23:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(764782, 80655, 4494, '<td valign="top">Peggy, it was really tough to get the whole thing in focus.  I used a 28mm (or less) teleconverter lens, and the highest Fstop possible.  Then I moved back as far as possible and took about 20 or 30 shots, focusing on all different parts of the guitar until I saw a pic that looked focused on the entire length.<br/> <br/>The great color on the guitar came from the walls of my living room area which is kind of a tan/yellowish color!  And the light was natural (right side) from the sliding doors to the outside.<br/> <br/>Glad you like it!<br/></td>', 'Peggy, it was really tough to get the whole thing in focus.  I used a 28mm (or less) teleconverter lens, and the highest Fstop possible.  Then I moved back as far as possible and took about 20 or 30 shots, focusing on all different parts of the guitar until I saw a pic that looked focused on the entire length. The great color on the guitar came from the walls of my living room area which is kind of a tan/yellowish color!  And the light was natural (right side) from the sliding doors to the outside. Glad you like it!', '2004-06-16 00:23:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(765480, 81069, 472, '<td valign="top">one of the coolest shots i''ve seen on dpc in a while.  congrats.</td>', 'one of the coolest shots i''ve seen on dpc in a while.  congrats.', '2004-06-16 09:00:58.000000', NULL, 0),
