(1529749, 81181, 12253, '<td valign="top">Landscape class exercise "analysis" (more critical than the usual DPC comment): <br/> <br/>Hits.  I love the perspective you chose for this shot.  The inclusion of the lamp works very well and gives this great depth.  The color of the buildings across the shore and the clouds are also exceptional.<br/> <br/>Misses.  Technically, it''s exceptional.  Subjectively--aesthetically--to me, this is a mostly cloud shot, and while the clouds and each of the other elements are exceptionally well presented, overall, it misses the beauty/peaceful/wow mark one can assign to the greatest landscapes.  That''s just my own personal "feeling" from this, as we all are "affected" by art.</td>', 'Landscape class exercise "analysis" (more critical than the usual DPC comment):  Hits.  I love the perspective you chose for this shot.  The inclusion of the lamp works very well and gives this great depth.  The color of the buildings across the shore and the clouds are also exceptional. Misses.  Technically, it''s exceptional.  Subjectively--aesthetically--to me, this is a mostly cloud shot, and while the clouds and each of the other elements are exceptionally well presented, overall, it misses the beauty/peaceful/wow mark one can assign to the greatest landscapes.  That''s just my own personal "feeling" from this, as we all are "affected" by art.', '2005-07-12 12:51:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1558102, 81606, 37893, '<td valign="top">There are actually two blue windows :) Too much building and not enough sky Bob. If the airplane was part of the composition then I would have probably given it a little more breathing room. Great DOF!<br/> <br/>Edit: I do like the symmetry of the image. it''s a dull building. Ho-hum in my books but the vanishing points and leading lines towards the plane is great.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-07-23 23:36:29.</i></td>', 'There are actually two blue windows :) Too much building and not enough sky Bob. If the airplane was part of the composition then I would have probably given it a little more breathing room. Great DOF! Edit: I do like the symmetry of the image. it''s a dull building. Ho-hum in my books but the vanishing points and leading lines towards the plane is great.', '2005-07-24 00:35:21.000000', '2005-07-24 00:36:29.000000', 0),
